# SplitPlate — Backend (Firebase)

SplitPlate uses **Firebase Firestore** as its backend — a serverless NoSQL cloud database. No custom server is needed.

---

## Firebase Project Details

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Project ID | `splitplat` |
| Console | https://console.firebase.google.com/project/splitplat |
| Database | Cloud Firestore (default) |

---

## Setup — Firestore Rules

Go to **Firebase Console → Firestore Database → Rules tab** → paste this → click **Publish**:

```
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if true;
    }
  }
}
```

---

## Database Structure

```
Firestore
└── users/
    └── {emailKey}/
        ├── uid
        ├── name
        ├── email
        ├── password       ← SHA-256 hashed
        ├── createdAt
        ├── lastLogin
        └── orders/
            └── {orderId}/
                ├── grandTotal
                ├── restaurants[]
                ├── cart[]
                ├── people[]
                ├── perPersonDetails{}
                ├── payState{}
                ├── refundState{}
                └── updatedAt
```

---

## Email Key Convention

Firebase document IDs cannot contain `.` or `@` so emails are converted:

```
jishu@gmail.com  →  jishu_at_gmail_com
anya@gmail.com   →  anya_at_gmail_com
```

---

## Security

| Feature | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Password storage | SHA-256 hashed using `crypto.subtle.digest` |
| Input sanitisation | `sanitise()` escapes `<>` before innerHTML |
| Firestore rules | Open for demo — restrict per user in production |
| Debounced writes | 1000ms debounce prevents Firebase quota exhaustion |

